    "step:prime-root": {
      "title": "A prime is not a square",
      "summary": "If a natural prime p were k², then p > 1 would force k > 1. The equality p = k·k would make k a divisor strictly between 1 and p. This contradicts primality, so the natural square criterion applies.",
      "areas": [
